---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Field Notes — GeoSmart" description="Field notes, geological explanations and learning notes from Camila Fernández on geology, Norway, subsurface and scientific curiosity.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-kicker">Geology · Norway · Learning</div>
      <h1>Field Notes</h1>
      <p class="muted">The curious side of GeoSmart: geological ideas, observations, explanations and lessons from learning to read the Earth.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container field-notes-layout">
      <article class="note-feature note-article-card">
        <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Geophysics</span><span>·</span><span>First note</span></div>
        <h2>Why does seismic interpretation actually matter?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Seismic data is more than pretty lines on a screen. It is a way of asking geological questions about structures and histories we cannot see directly.</p>
        <div class="article-teaser"><span>WHAT I’LL EXPLORE</span><p>Reflections · horizons · faults · geological reasoning · uncertainty</p></div>
        <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 01</span><span>In preparation</span></div>
      </article>

      <div class="note-list note-grid">
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Norway</span><span>Field · Trondheim</span></div>
          <h3>Geology in Trondheim</h3>
          <p>What changes when you start looking at an everyday landscape with a geologist's eye — and what I am noticing around Trondheim.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 02</span><span>In preparation</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Sedimentology</span><span>Learning</span></div>
          <h3>Reading a sedimentary log</h3>
          <p>How observations become a sedimentary interpretation, and why the geological story is rarely as simple as one neat answer.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 03</span><span>In preparation</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Energy</span><span>Subsurface</span></div>
          <h3>What makes a good reservoir?</h3>
          <p>Porosity, permeability and the geological history behind reservoir quality — without drowning in jargon.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 04</span><span>In preparation</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="note note-card">
          <div class="note-meta"><span class="card-tag">Learning</span><span>Student life</span></div>
          <h3>Things I wish I knew before studying geology</h3>
          <p>Fieldwork, maps, software, mistakes and the gradual process of learning how to think like a geologist.</p>
          <div class="note-footer"><span>Field Note 05</span><span>In preparation</span></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
